12
This set of IDs ranges from September 23, 2020 to January 8, 2021 and consists of 215,923 unique tweet IDs. As of November 15, 2022, there are only 35,552 (16.47%) of the original number of tweets retrievable via the API.", "location": "Section 4 (Case Study: Implications for Replicating Sensitive Twitter Studies), lines 205-208", "reason": "Although the author uses the term 'replication', the study rehydrates the original 215,923 tweet IDs and auxiliary data from Kim's (2023) replication archive to re-run the original analyses on the surviving subset of original observations rather than collecting a new sample, making it a reproduction under the codebook.", "method": "argon"}, "outcome": {"quote": "Comparing the original model 5 with regressions using the recrawled dataset (see Figure
6
) reveals that one of the paper’s key findings of having more women targeted by violent tweets does not hold anymore. The estimate of the effect is close to zero, and the coefficient’s 95% confidence interval of the recrawled model widely includes zero, too.", "location": "Section 4.2 (Replication: Statistical Model Findings), lines 287-289", "reason": "Re-running the original descriptive and regression analyses on the recrawled archive data produces comparable numerical output that differs considerably from the published figures, and nonrandom tweet attrition removes the key finding that women are disproportionately targeted by violent tweets.", "method": "argon"}}

