{"outcome_robustness": {"quote": "The claim selected for the original study yielded a negative regression interaction term in the focal test, corresponding to an increased local degree proportion reducing the effect of holding a four-year degree on the use of verbal skills. The replication yielded a positive regression interaction term in the focal test, corresponding to an effect in a different pattern compared to the original study.

Deviations from preregistration.
There were no deviations from the preregistration plan, or changes to the preregistered script (except to remove the line limiting analysis to a random 5% subset of the data).", "location": "Replication Result / Deviations from preregistration, lines 852-860", "reason": "The report conducts only a single preregistered reproduction attempt (Model 1) reconstructing the original analysis from the paper's description and raw data sources, which fails to recover the original negative interaction coefficient (coded on Axis 1 as 'computational issues'). The differences in sample restriction, occupation matching, and CFA construction are documented as unavoidable reconstruction deviations due to omitted details in the original paper and code rather than alternative specifications or sensitivity analyses tested by the reproducer. Because no robustness checks or alternative specifications were conducted, outcome_robustness is 'not checked'.", "method": "argon"}}

{"outcome_robustness": {"quote": "Focal test: A statistically significant association (p < .01) between the amount a player sent and participation in a laboratory experiment. The marginal effect indicates that for every additional $10 sent during the experiment, a student was, in absolute terms, 4.3 percent less likely to select into the lab.

Reproduction result: Analyst was able to reproduce the results after the extended PBR attempt – A statistically significant association (p < .01) between the amount a player sent and participation in a laboratory experiment. The marginal effect indicates that for every additional $10 sent during the experiment, a student was, in absolute terms, 4.3 percent less likely to select into the lab.

Deviations from the preregistration: There are no deviations from the preregistration.", "location": "fulltext, lines 10-14", "reason": "The primary report is a Push Button Reproduction (reproduction) of Cleave, Nikiforakis, and Slonim (2013) focused solely on computationally reproducing the original focal finding in Table 3, Column 4 and Column 4m. Under the codebook, 'not checked' applies when the text shows that the report only considered computational reproducibility and did not conduct robustness checks. Although the blind coding marked outcome_robustness as 'cannot_be_determined' because the analyst noted an 'outcome does not vary' error when trying to add 'session' to the probit model, the 'PBR troubleshooting details' section explicitly shows that the analyst only tried adding 'session' to check whether it corresponded to the 'order effects' mentioned in the original Table 3 notes while reconstructing the original specification, after already reproducing the exact Table 3 Column 4 and 4m results without it. Because this step was part of reconstructing the original model rather than testing alternative specifications for robustness, robustness was not checked.", "method": "argon"}}

